# What this file does: keeps private things out of this public showcase repository.
#
# It works the opposite way round from a normal ignore file. Instead of naming the
# things to keep out, it keeps EVERYTHING out and then lets back in only the handful
# of files this showcase is actually for. So anything new that ever lands in this
# folder -- a note, a config file, a key, a screenshot taken by accident -- stays on
# the laptop by default, even if you run "git add ." without looking at what it is.
#
# To publish something new here, add a line for it below. Nothing else gets out.

# Keep everything out.
*

# Let back in only the showcase itself.
!.gitignore
!README.md
!LICENSE

# ...and the pictures. The folder has to be let in first, then the pictures inside it.
# Anything in that folder which is not a .png stays out.
!images/
!images/*.png
